{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["And the days in which we walked from Kadesh-barnea — from the place of the sending of the spies, thirty-eight years, for in the second year he sent the spies." "The men of war — the twenty-year-olds who go out to the army. And I, the younger, say: 'the men of war' were those of whom it is said ויעפילו לעלות אל ראש ההר, as it says: ותחגרו איש את כלי מלחמתו. And Moshe said to them: לא תעלו ולא תלחמו. And similarly in Joshua it says: כי ארבעים שנה הלכו בני ישראל במדבר — עד תום כל הגוי אנשי המלחמה היוצאים ממצרים אשר לא שמעו בקול ה׳ אשר נשבע ה׳ להם לבלתי הראותם את הארץ אשר וגו׳ — and therefore he calls them 'the men of war' and does not say 'men of war' without specification, but rather 'the men of war' who are known to us, who transgressed the word of the Holy One, blessed be He; but the rest who fought against Sihon and Og he does not call 'the men of war,' for by the word of the Holy One, blessed be He, they fought, and they entered the land — for they were not yet twenty years old at the time of the first war in the second year, when the spies were sent."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:14.670777951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}